Z||000000||Cozmo||11-01-2001||09:31 PM||||I Started the car up, WTF the alt. squeals and the volts read about 8...<BR>Turn it off, what's that sound?<BR>The starter running <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"><BR>Mind you, the car is on a slope (uphill), in gear (1st., a 4 spd.) with no emergency brake (broken). I could see my car leaping forward into my buddy's Formula <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>I Jump out, open the trunk and disconnect the battery and the starter stops running (whew!)<BR>I Remember an old trick on Triumphs and get underneath the car and beat on the starter solenoid with a hammer, then hook the battery back up and all is good!<BR>So maybe I need a new solenoid?<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR> <P>------------------<BR><B>BobC</B><BR><B>'85 2M6 Targa</B><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/targsig.jpg"> <BR><B>Suncoast Fieros</B>||||reg||10
Z||000001||Tigger||11-01-2001||09:53 PM||||Get a new starter!!!<P>Before you ruin the teeth on the flywheel.<P>Had this happen to me, once.  Yanked the starter as soon as I got home.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 11-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||x-thumpr-x||11-01-2001||10:13 PM||||Hmm had this happen to me once. I was working under the car trying to find out why my car won't start! then suddenly the car's starter kicked in while I was underneath the car. GASP!  Talk about kickstarting your heart! I found the problem, the wire fron the ignition to the starter had some sheilding rubbed off. At first it was grounding out on a heat sheild, but when the car's starter kicked in, it was lying across the the positive terminal line on the starter. <P>i don't think I ever got out from under a car so fast and disconnect the battery.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">||||reg||1
